    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d190">

                <pb facs="0283" n="177" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg177"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Egan to Mr.
                            Blaine</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-09-30"><hi rendition="#italic">September 30,
                            1891</hi>.</date> (Received October 1.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Egan states that in a note sent him the minister for foreign affairs refuses
                    safe-conduct or permission to refugees to leave the country, and maintains the
                    correctness of all that has been done by the authorities. The minister for
                    foreign affairs also repeats the unfounded and absurd charges of the refugees
                    conspiring in the United States legation. Since Saturday the trouble to the
                    legation had ceased, and no more arrests had been made.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
